{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Behold.</b> Most of the commentators said that \"My servant\" is the righteous of Israel, and the Gaon [Saadia] said that it is Cyrus, but the correct view in my eyes is that it is the prophet, and he speaks on behalf of his own soul, as he mentioned: \"and I gave you as a light of nations\" (Isaiah 49:6):" "<b>I have given My spirit.</b> The spirit of prophecy:" "<b>Judgment.</b> These are the things to come; whatever will happen to every nation, he will declare it. And according to the view of the Gaon [Saadia], that Cyrus will be a king of righteousness:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "Resolved the ms. abbreviation עבדיהם to the marginal correction עבדי הם ('My servant') per the צ\"ל notation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:30.326102406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}